      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "recto",
          "value": "\n<ol><li>[By Your Name, O Me]rciful One. The text of a marriage contract.</li>\n<li>[On such day] of the week, such and such of month</li>\n<li>[X,] four thousand, eight</li>\n<li>[hundred and] fifty[-four] years A.</li>\n<li>M., [in] town X, which is adjacent to place</li>\n<li>X, on river (X), \"I, Saadia the [\u1e25azza]n</li>\n<li>b. R. \u1e62edaqa the [\u1e25azza]n, m(ay his) s(oul be) b(ound) i(n the bundle of) l(ife), declare</li>\n<li>intentionally, wi[lling]ly, and of my choice to marry</li>\n<li>you, thee, \u02bfAz\u016bz, the bride, daughter of master</li>\n<li>Isaac (who) r(ests in) E(den), so that you shall be my wife. I</li>\n<li>will serve, nourish, [h]onor, and support you</li>\n<li>in the manner of Jewish men who serve, nourish,</li>\n<li>provide for, and honor their wives</li>\n<li>faithfully. And you \u02bfAz\u016bz daughter of Isaac (who) r(ests in) E(den)</li>\n<li>shall stand before (me) and serve me. And you shall strive</li>\n<li>to do with me all that do</li>\n<li>proper women wi[th] their husbands, in purity</li></ol>\n",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
